Package: marbounds
Title: Bounds on Causal Effects with Mixed Informative and Non-Informative Missingness
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Max", "Rubinstein", email = "mrubinstein@rand.org", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Denis", "Agniel", email = "dagniel@rand.org", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Implements influence-function-based estimators for bounds on causal effects
  (ATE, composite ATE, separable direct effect) when outcomes are missing due to an
  unknown mixture of informative and non-informative missingness. Supports both the
  original binary-outcome models and continuous-outcome global L2 sensitivity models
  for informative missingness and unmeasured confounding. Continuous-outcome tools
  include closed-form outer bounds, empirical sharp sieve-dual bounds, reduced-form
  net-missingness bounds, sensitivity grids, tipping frontiers, and simulation.
  Nuisance functions are estimated with cross-fitting. Sharp continuous-outcome
  endpoints support both plug-in and augmented doubly robust evaluation. A
  standalone cross-fitted augmented inverse-probability weighted estimator
  provides point estimation under MAR and no unmeasured confounding.
  The package also implements reduced-form influence-function estimators,
  multiplier simultaneous bands, L-infinity outer and sharp-sieve comparisons,
  capped L2 prevalence bounds for binary composite and separable effects,
  covariate-omission calibration with combined influence-function frontier
  bands, and simulation tools for comparing endpoint
  bias and coverage. Prespecified simulation-study drivers vary overlap,
  missingness prevalence and severity, nuisance complexity, concentration,
  and outcome tails, and separately assess AIPW calibration benchmarks.
